    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0024" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">855A.24/50: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the Belgian
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-17T19:45:00-04:00">August 17,
                            1942—7:45 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–22. Department’s airgram A–17, August 12. Department informed that export
                    duties have recently been increased in Belgian <pb facs="0025" n="19"
                        xml:id="pg19"/> Congo on palm nuts and oil of geranium. Please consider
                    advisability of suggesting paragraph in tripartite agreement providing that
                    Congo export duties shall not be increased during term of agreement on
                    commodities listed in the agreement as of interest to us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
